      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## QuantFunc Krea-2\n\n- **QuantFunc Krea-2 Loader** replaces the official `Load Diffusion Model` (UNETLoader): the QuantFunc engine runs the Krea-2 Turbo transformer; the text encoder (`CLIPLoader`, type `krea2`), the VAE and the sampler stay stock ComfyUI.\n- `transformer`: `krea2-turbo-quantfunc-int4-r128.safetensors` (or the smaller `krea2-turbo-quantfunc-int4-r32.safetensors`) from ModelScope [QuantFunc/Krea-2-QuantFunc-4bit](https://modelscope.cn/models/QuantFunc/Krea-2-QuantFunc-4bit), in `models/diffusion_models`.\n- Text encoder `qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors` and VAE `qwen_image_vae.safetensors`: Hugging Face [Comfy-Org/Krea-2](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2).\n- `quality_enhance`: OFF (default) is faster; ON gives the highest quality.\n- Krea-2 Turbo is guidance-distilled: 8 steps, CFG 1, euler / simple, and the negative prompt is zeroed (`ConditioningZero Out`).\n\n**Two passes (double sampling).** The first KSampler makes the image at 1024x1024; `Upscale Latent By` enlarges the latent 1.5x and the second KSampler refines it at 1536x1536 (4 steps, denoise 0.4). A lower denoise keeps more of the first image.\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## QuantFunc Krea-2\n\n- **QuantFunc Krea-2 Loader** replaces the official `Load Diffusion Model` (UNETLoader): the QuantFunc engine runs the Krea-2 Turbo transformer; the text encoder (`CLIPLoader`, type `krea2`), the VAE and the sampler stay stock ComfyUI.\n- `transformer`: `krea2-turbo-quantfunc-int4-r128.safetensors` (or the smaller `krea2-turbo-quantfunc-int4-r32.safetensors`) from ModelScope [QuantFunc/Krea-2-QuantFunc-4bit](https://modelscope.cn/models/QuantFunc/Krea-2-QuantFunc-4bit), in `models/diffusion_models`.\n- Text encoder `qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors` and VAE `qwen_image_vae.safetensors`: Hugging Face [Comfy-Org/Krea-2](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2).\n- `quality_enhance`: OFF (default) is faster; ON gives the highest quality.\n- Krea-2 Turbo is guidance-distilled: 8 steps, CFG 1, euler / simple, and the negative prompt is zeroed (`ConditioningZero Out`).\n\n**Two passes (double sampling).** The first KSampler makes the image at 1024x1024; `Upscale Latent By` enlarges the latent 1.5x and the second KSampler refines it at 1536x1536 (4 steps, denoise 0.4). A lower denoise keeps more of the first image.\n"
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
